‎  "title": "CHAPTER 3: LEARNING AND THEORIES OF LEARNING",
‎  "content": "<b><font color='#2E7D32'>ውድ የሀገሬ ልጆች እንዲሁም የEthioFresh ቤተሰቦች! 💖👋 እንደምን አላችሁ? ዛሬ የGeneral Psychology (Psyc 1011) Chapter 3 Part 1 Tutorial ይዘንላችሁ መጥተናል። በዚህ ክፍል ስለ Learning ምንነት፣ Characteristics፣ Principles፣ Factors እና Classical Conditioning Theory በዝርዝር እናያለን። ፈተና ላይ 100% ውጤታማ የሚያደርጓችሁ ዝርዝር ነጥቦች፣ የሳይኮሎጂ ቀልዶች እና የፈተና ትሪኮች ተካተዋል!👇👇👇</font></b><br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>3.1. Definition, Characteristics and Principles of Learning</font></b><br><br><b>3.1.1. Definitions of Learning</b><br>Learning is defined as a <b>relatively permanent change in behavior occurring as a result of experience or practice</b>.<br><br>The definition emphasizes key attributes of learning:<br>1. <b>Learning is a change in behavior:</b> It involves acquiring new ways of doing things or modifying existing responses.<br>2. <b>This change in behavior is relatively permanent:</b> Temporary changes (like reaction to fatigue or drugs) do not count as learning.<br>3. <b>Exclusions from learning:</b> It does not include changes due to illness, fatigue, maturation, or the use of intoxicants.<br>4. <b>Not due to biological factors alone:</b> Permanent changes brought on solely by biological factors (like hormonal changes) are not classified as learning; it must stem from experience or practice.<br>5. <b>Not directly observable:</b> Learning is an internal process that manifests indirectly through the performance and activities of an individual.<br><br>👉 <b>የመማር (Learning) ብያኔ:</b><br>መማር ማለት <b>በልምድ (Experience) ወይም ልምምድ (Practice) ምክንያት የሚመጣ በአንፃራዊነት ዘላቂ የሆነ የባህሪ ለውጥ</b> ነው። <br>• <b>የባህሪ ለውጥ:</b> አዲስ ነገር ማወቅ ወይም አሰራር መቀየርን ያካትታል።<br>• <b>አንፃራዊ ዘላቂነት:</b> በድካም ወይም በመድኃኒት ምክንያት የሚመጣ ጊዜያዊ ለውጥ መማር አይባልም።<br>• <b>ከመማር የማይቆጠሩ:</b> የህመም፣ የድካም፣ የእድገት (Maturation) እና የአልኮል/ዕፅ ተፅዕኖዎች መማር አይደሉም።<br>• <b>ቀጥታ አይታይም:</b> መማር በአእምሮ ውስጥ የሚካሄድ ሲሆን የሚታየው ሰውየው በተግባር ሲያሳየው (Performance) ብቻ ነው።<br><br>😂 <b>የሳይኮሎጂ ቀልድ ለፈገግታ:</b> አንድ ተማሪ ዶርም ውስጥ ተኝቶ \"እንዴ አልጠራሁም እንዴ?\" ሲል... ጓደኛው \"ምን እያደረክ ነው?\" ቢለው... \"አእምሮዬ በውስጥ እየተማረ (Learning is not directly observable) ስለሆነ ነው በተግባር የማይታየው!\" አለው ይባላል! 😂<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>3.1.2. Characteristics of Learning</font></b><br><br>According to Yoakman and Simpson, the major important characteristics of learning are:<br>1. <b>Continuous modification of behavior throughout life:</b> Learning happens from birth to death.<br>2. <b>Pervasive:</b> It reaches into all aspects of human life (habits, skills, attitudes).<br>3. <b>Involves the whole person:</b> Engages an individual socially, emotionally, and intellectually.<br>4. <b>Change in the organization of experiences:</b> Reorganizing prior knowledge with new information.<br>5. <b>Responsive to incentives:</b> Driven and modified by rewards, goals, or motivation.<br>6. <b>Active process:</b> Requires active engagement from the learner.<br>7. <b>Purposeful:</b> Focused on achieving specific goals.<br>8. <b>Depends on maturation, motivation, and practice:</b> Readiness and practice are crucial.<br>9. <b>Multifaceted:</b> Learners acquire knowledge, attitudes, and physical skills simultaneously.<br><br>👉 <b>የመማር ባህሪያት (Characteristics of Learning):</b><br>• <b>ቀጣይነት ያለው (Continuous):</b> በህይወታችን ሙሉ ከልጅነት እስከ ዕድሜ ልክ የሚቀጥል ነው።<br>• <b>ሁሉን አቀፍ (Pervasive):</b> የህይወታችንን ሁሉንም ክፍሎች (ልማድ፣ ክህሎት፣ አስተሳሰብ) ይነካል።<br>• <b>ሙሉ ሰውን ያሳትፋል:</b> በማህበራዊ፣ በስሜት እና በአእምሮ ደረጃ ያሳታፈል።<br>• <b>ንቁ ሂደት (Active Process):</b> ተማሪው በራሱ ጥረትና ተሳትፎ የሚያደርገው ነው።<br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>3.1.3. Principles of Learning</font></b><br><br>Key principles explaining how learning occurs effectively:<br>• <b>Readiness:</b> Individuals learn best when they are physically, mentally, and emotionally ready to learn.<br>• <b>Exercise/Practice:</b> Students learn best and retain information longer when they have meaningful practice and exercise.<br>• <b>Effect:</b> Learning is strengthened when accompanied by a pleasant or satisfying feeling, and weakened when associated with an unpleasant feeling.<br>• <b>Primacy:</b> Things learned first create a strong impression in the mind that is difficult to erase.<br>• <b>Recency:</b> Things most recently learned are best remembered.<br>• <b>Intensity:</b> Students learn more from the real thing than from a substitute.<br>• <b>Required Abilities:</b> Individuals must have basic abilities and skills that help them learn.<br>• <b>Freedom:</b> Things freely learned are best learned; greater freedom yields higher intellectual and moral advancement.<br><br>👉   Principles of Learning:<br>• <b>ዝግጁነት (Readiness):</b> በአካል፣ በአእምሮና በስሜት ዝግጁ ስንሆን ትምህርት ይገባናል።<br>• <b>ልምምድ (Exercise):</b> በደንብ ሲለማመዱት መረጃው በአእምሮ ውስጥ ቆይቶ ይኖራል።<br>• <b>ውጤት (Effect):</b> የመማሩ ሂደት ደስ የሚል ስሜት ካለው መማሩ ይጎለብታል፤ ደስ የማይል ከሆነ ይዳከማል።<br>• <b>መጀመሪያ የተማሩት (Primacy):</b> መጀመሪያ የተማሩት ነገር አእምሮ ውስጥ በጥብቅ ይያዛል።<br>• <b>የቅርብ ጊዜ (Recency):</b> በቅርብ የተማሩት ነገር አይረሳም።<br><br><font color='#E65100'>💡 <b>Exam Hint:</b></font> ፈተና ላይ \"ተማሪዎች ከፎቶ ይልቅ እውነተኛውን እቃ አይተው ሲማሩ በደንብ ይገባቸዋል\" የሚለው የትኛው Principle ነው ከተባላችሁ መልሱ <b>Principle of Intensity</b> ነው! <br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>3.2. Factors Influencing Learning</font></b><br><br>Factors affecting the effectiveness of learning include:<br>1. <b>Motivation:</b> Stronger and clearer motives lead to greater effort and enthusiasm.<br>2. <b>Maturation:</b> Neuro-muscular coordination is necessary before learning a task (e.g., a child must mature physically before learning to walk).<br>3. <b>Health condition of the learner:</b> Sensory defects, malnutrition, lack of sleep, and fatigue hinder learning.<br>4. <b>Psychological wellbeing:</b> Worries, fears, loneliness, and inferiority hinder learning, whereas self-confidence and self-reliance facilitate it.<br>5. <b>Good working conditions:</b> Fresh air, proper lighting, comfortable temperature, and absence of noise promote learning.<br>6. <b>Background experiences:</b> Prior knowledge affects the understanding of new concepts.<br>7. <b>Length of the working period:</b> Extremely long sessions cause fatigue, while excessively short sessions prevent mastery.<br>8. <b>Massed vs. Distributed learning:</b> Spreading learning across time with reasonable rest gaps (distributed) brings better results than cramming all at once (massed).<br><br>👉 <b>በመማር ላይ ተፅዕኖ የሚያሳድሩ ሁኔታዎች:</b><br>• <b>ተነሳሽነት (Motivation):</b> ፍላጎት በጨመረ ቁጥር የመማር ብቃት ይጨምራል።<br>• <b>ዕድገት (Maturation):</b> ለአንድ ተግባር የአካልና የአእምሮ ዝግጁነት ያስፈልጋል (ለምሳሌ ህፃን ሳይጎለምስ መሄድ አይችልም)።<br>• <b>ጤና እና አእምሯዊ ሰላም:</b> እንቅልፍ ማጣት፣ ጭንቀት እና ፍርሃት መማርን ይከለክላሉ።<br>• <b>Distributed Learning vs Massed Learning:</b> ፈተናን ከሳምንታት በፊት ከፋፍሎ ማጥናት (Distributed)፣ ፈተና ዋዜማ ሌሊቱን ሙሉ ከማደር (Massed/Cramming) በጣም ውጤታማ ያደርጋል! <br><br><hr><br><b><font color='#1565C0'>3.3. Theories of Learning and their Applications</font></b><br><br>Learning theories explore the mechanisms behind behavior change. Learning theories are conceptual frameworks that describe how information is absorbed, processed, and retained during learning. Cognitive, emotional, and environmental influences, as well as prior experience, all play a part in how understanding, or a world view, is acquired or changed and knowledge and skills retained. The major categories include behavioral, observational, and cognitive theories.<br><br><b>3.3.1. Behavioral Theory of Learning</b><br>Behavioral theories view learning as a result of <b>stimulus-response (S-R) associations</b>, focusing strictly on observable behavior. Behaviorism assumes that a learner is essentially passive, responding to environmental stimuli. The learner starts off with a clean slate (i.e. tabula rasa) and behavior is shaped through positive reinforcement or negative reinforcement.<br><br><b>3.3.1.1. Classical Conditioning Theory</b><br>Pioneered by Ivan Pavlov, classical conditioning focuses on learning <b>involuntary emotional or physiological responses</b> to stimuli. It pairs a neutral stimulus with an unconditioned stimulus to elicit a response.<br><br><b>Basic Terms in Classical Conditioning:</b><br>• <b>Neutral Stimulus (NS):</b> A stimulus that initially brings no targeted response (e.g., Bell sound before training).<br>• <b>Unconditioned Stimulus (UCS):</b> A stimulus that naturally and automatically triggers an unlearned response (e.g., Food).<br>• <b>Unconditioned Response (UCR):</b> An automatic, unlearned natural reaction to the UCS (e.g., Salivation to food).<br>• <b>Conditioned Stimulus (CS):</b> A previously neutral stimulus that, after association with UCS, triggers a response (e.g., Bell sound after training).<br>• <b>Conditioned Response (CR):</b> The learned response to a previously neutral stimulus (e.g., Salivation to bell sound).<br><br><b>Pavlov's Experiment Stages:</b><br>1. <i>Before Training:</i> CS (Bell) ➔ No Response | UCS (Food) ➔ UCR (Salivation)<br>2. <i>During Training:</i> CS (Bell) + UCS (Food) ➔ UCR (Salivation)<br>3. <i>After Training:</i> CS (Bell) ➔ CR (Salivation)<br><br>👉 <b>Classical Conditioning Theory (የፓቭሎቭ ንድፈ-ሀሳብ):</b><br>ይህ Theory የሚያተኩረው <b>ኢ-ፈቃደኛ (Involuntary) የሆኑ የፊዚዮሎጂ ወይም የስሜት ምላሾችን</b> ከአዲስ ነገር ጋር በማመዳመድ (Association) መማር ላይ ነው።<br>• <b>UCS (ምግብ):</b> ያለምንም ስልጠና በተፈጥሮ ምላሽ የሚያመጣ።<br>• <b>UCR (ምራቅ ማፍሰስ):</b> ለምግብ የሚሰጥ ተፈጥሯዊ ምላሽ።<br>• <b>CS (ደወል):</b> ከምግብ ጋር ከተለመደ በኋላ ምላሽ ማስገኘት የቻለ።<br>• <b>CR (ለደወል ምራቅ ማፍሰስ):</b> በስልጠና/በልምድ የተገኘ ምላሽ።<br><br><b>Principles of Classical Conditioning:</b><br>• <b>Stimulus Generalization:</b> Responding in the same way to similar stimuli (e.g., Dog salivating to a doorbell or phone ring, thinking it's the dinner bell).<br>• <b>Stimulus Discrimination:</b> Differentiating between similar stimuli (e.g., Dog salivating ONLY to the specific dinner bell).<br>• <b>Extinction:</b> The gradual weakening and disappearance of CR when CS is repeatedly presented without UCS.<br>• <b>Spontaneous Recovery:</b> The reemergence of an extinguished conditioned response after a period of rest without further conditioning.<br><br>👉 <b>Classical Conditioning :</b><br>• <b>Stimulus Generalization:</b> ይመሳሰላሉ ተብለው ለተለያዩ ነገሮች ተመሳሳይ ምላሽ መስጠት (ለምሳሌ፡ ለስልክ ጥሪ እና ለበር ደወል እኩል ምራቅ ማፍሰስ)።<br>• <b>Stimulus Discrimination:</b> ተመሳሳይ ነገሮችን ለይቶ ማወቅ (ለምሳሌ፡ ለምግብ ደወል ብቻ ምራቅ ማፍሰስ)።<br>• <b>Extinction (ጠፋ):</b> ደወሉ እየተደወለ ምግብ ካልቀረበ ምራቅ ማፍሰሱ ቀስ በቀስ ይጠፋል።<br>• <b>Spontaneous Recovery:</b> ከዕረፍት በኋላ የጠፋው ባህሪ ድንገት ተመልሶ ብቅ ማለት።<br><br><font color='#E65100'>💡 <b>Exam Case Exercise:</b></font><br><i>Question:</i> A 1-year-old child touches an electrical outlet with a toy, gets shocked, and cries. Later, the child shows fear whenever the mother gives him that toy. Identify:<br>a) <b>UCS:</b> Electric Shock<br>b) <b>UCR:</b> Fear/Crying from shock<br>c) <b>CS:</b> The Toy<br>d) <b>CR:</b> Fear of the toy<br><br><br><b><font color='#2E7D32'>🌸 💖 ውድ የEthioFresh አባላት፣ የPsychology Chapter 3 Part 1 በዚሁ ተጠናቋል! በዚህ ክፍል ስለ Learning Definitions፣ Principles፣ Factors እና Classical Conditioning አይተናል። ቀጣይ Part 2 ላይ Operant Conditioning እና ሌሎችንም በሰፊው ይዘንላችሁ እንመጣለን። መልካም የጥናት ጊዜ ይሁንላችሁ!</font></b>"
‎}
